if(view==='network'){let n=await api('network');c.innerHTML='<div class="grid"><section class="panel pad"><h2>Broadcasting & listening</h2><div class="stats" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr"><div class="stat"><span class="kicker">Desktop HTTP</span><strong>'+location.port+'</strong><small>127.0.0.1 · local interface</small></div><div class="stat"><span class="kicker">Engine bus TCP</span><strong>'+n.tcp_port+'</strong><small>'+esc(n.tcp_host)+'</small></div></div><p>UDP discovery: port '+n.discovery_port+' · scope: '+esc(n.scope)+'. Discovery broadcasts announce the app and its port every ten seconds. Engine results travel only to authenticated TCP subscribers.</p><p>Use Start Neural App LAN.cmd to expose the engine bus and discovery to your LAN. The desktop HTTP interface stays local.</p><div class="actions"><button id="showBusKey">Show connection key</button></div><pre id="busKey" hidden></pre></section><section class="panel pad"><h2>Connect another program</h2><p>Connect to TCP '+n.tcp_port+' and send one JSON line. Use your key from the connection panel.</p><pre>{"token":"YOUR_CONNECTION_KEY","op":"publish","section":"pipeline","data":{"text":"Shared input"}}\n\n{"token":"YOUR_CONNECTION_KEY","op":"result","id":"RETURNED_JOB_ID"}\n\n{"token":"YOUR_CONNECTION_KEY","op":"subscribe"}</pre><p>Subscribers receive result events with receipt identifiers. Publish and poll the job to retrieve the full result. Discovery request: send NEURAL_DISCOVER to UDP '+n.discovery_port+'.</p></section></div>';bind('showBusKey',async()=>{$('#busKey').hidden=false;$('#busKey').textContent=(await api('bus-key')).key});return}
